    "title": "Swinging into spring at Enger Park Golf Course - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By WDIO ,\n1 days ago\nEnger Park Golf Course opened for the season on Tuesday. Sunshine and warm temperatures drew in a full tee sheet of golfers.\nCraig Smith from the Enger Park Golf Course told WDIO, “Customers are chomping at the bit to get out there,” especially after a cool spring and the two recent snow storms.\nCurrently, only the front nine holes and the driving range are open while crews clear remaining snow and debris before reopening all 18 holes.\nSmith said course conditions will keep improving and that this season will not be impacted by construction like last year\nEnger Park is open from 10 a.m. to 6 p.m. to allow for morning frost, and more tee times are expected as temperatures rise.\nEnger Park is the City of Duluth’s only public golf course. More details about the course online.",
